  "caveats": [
    "Each result is one discrete post-GC live-registry sample. Max-scanned/max-observed means the largest recorded sample, not a true peak between collections.",
    "allocations_cumulative_at_sample is an allocation ordinal, not live residency, allocated bytes, or an allocation-rate measure.",
    "Total and family inventories count successfully borrowed scanned objects. untracked_birth_sites limits source-site interpretation; do not infer that tracked birth sites cover all globals or attribute every untracked object to one specific cap.",
    "unavailable_borrows are reported separately and are not included as successfully inventoried objects.",
    "Vector reserved capacity and capacity-bytes do not measure allocator overhead, total heap, RSS, or achievable savings. Eligibility is a census condition, not a prediction that a compact representation is semantically or operationally safe.",
    "Diagnostic runs exited successfully but are not acceptance timings and establish no speed or memory improvement.",
    "Census eligibility is not prototype admission: the current compact prototype excludes canonical-index entries, symbol-sidecar objects, and arrays, and initially admits only plain templates.",
    "The diagnostic holes count is an internal Value::Empty-tag count, not proof of semantic property absence for every backing; classic-index reads can retain a descriptor.",
    "Dense inline active-prefix bucket 0 includes sidecars with values moved to heap storage and is not a count of empty JavaScript arrays."
  ],
